ntally come out at the  wrong metro station  and you find yourself being arrested for  being at the wrong time at the wrong  place  president alexander lukashenko told  russian tv his  26 years in power may have been too long  but says he won't step down  he again spoke of interference from the  west suggesting he's being watched by  american satellites  since the disputed election he has  looked east to moscow for support  the protesters of belarus stuck in the  middle insist  they just want free and fair elections  redmond shannon global news  london this is what driving through san  francisco looks like right now coming up  the fires  ripping through the west coast  drivers across utah witnessed this  yesterday at least 45 semi trucks were  blown over by hurricane force winds of  more than 120 kilometers an hour  four drivers were hospitalized officials  say many of the drivers had ignored  warnings  about the high winds powerful winds  along the u.s west coast are whipping up  flames and preventing  fire crews from containing a line of  fires that now stretches  from california to just south of the  canadian border the smoke has triggered  air quality advisories for the vancouver  area and other regions  in southwestern british columbia the  situation on the ground in parts of  washington state is dire  and one town a fire destroyed 80 percent  of buildings  including the local fire station  and this explosion in oregon happened  last night as a wildfire roared along a  highway south of portland  thousands of people have been forced  from their homes the record-setting  outbreak of fires in the state has  scorched more than 80 thousand hectares  of land  in california about 10 times that much  land has burned and thousands of homes  and businesses have been destroyed  and the smoke made for an eerie site in  san francisco  bay area residents woke up to this a  blanket of thick orange haze  blocking the morning light people in  some areas reported ash  falling li